 "char": {
  "id": "ray2",
  "handle": "ray_saw_the_lights",
  "name": "Ray",
  "bio": "Grew up under the Nevada sky.",
  "voice": "am_eric",
  "case": "roswell",
  "look": {
   "skin": "#b07850",
   "hair": "#2a2018",
   "style": "cap",
   "shirt": "#a8462e",
   "glasses": false,
   "extra": "none"
  },
  "script": "Every Nevada kid knows Roswell, even though it's in New Mexico. July 1947. The army air base put out a press release saying it had recovered a flying disc. The next day, it was a weather balloon. That backpedal fed fifty years of alien stories. In 1994, the Air Force finally said what it really was. Project Mogul. A secret balloon built to listen for Soviet nuclear tests. So it was a cover-up. Just not of aliens."
 },
